Notes are markdown pages that outlive any card: architecture, runbooks,
conventions. Notes belong to the current project; -p global addresses the
org-wide ones. A note is addressed by its slug, or by its id. Link with [[card:42]]
or [[note:slug]] in the body (decisions are cards, so [[card:7]] covers them). Every edit keeps the old text: see 'note history'.

Examples:
  lorvik note ls
  lorvik note show architecture
  lorvik note new runbook --title "Runbook" -b "How to deploy"
  lorvik note history runbook
  lorvik note show runbook --version 2

Usage
  lorvik note [flags]
  lorvik note [command]

Aliases
  note, notes

Commands
  archive     Archive a note (or restore it with --undo)
  edit        Change a note's title, body or page
  history     List the past versions of a note
  ls          List notes
  new         Create a note
  search      Search notes
  show        Show a note

Flags
  -h, --help   help for note

Global flags
      --api-url string   Server URL (default: LORVIK_API_URL)
      --json             Output the raw API JSON
  -p, --project string   Project slug (default: LORVIK_PROJECT or .lorvik.toml)
  -Q, --quiet            Suppress the unread notice on stderr and an empty inbox
      --session string   Session label for this chat (default: LORVIK_SESSION or derived; see lorvik session)

Run 'lorvik note <command> --help' for more information about a command.
